WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.430
- [Instructor] This here is a screenshot

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.360
from this exercise on Khan Academy.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.360
It says, the number 48 is
six times as many as eight.

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.860
Write this comparison as
a multiplication equation.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.170
So, pause this video and see
if you can have a go at that.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.740
All right, so, it sounds very fancy.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.720
This comparison as a
multiplication equation.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.000
But really they're just asking us

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.640
to write this as an equation.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.030
And if we were on Khan Academy
we would type it in here

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:27.870
but I'm just going to do it,

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:28.790
this is a screenshot,

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.890
so I'm just going to do it by digital pen.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:34.440
So, they're saying the number 48,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.150
the number 48,

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.087
and when they say is,

00:00:38.087 --> 00:00:40.170
another way of interpreting is to say,

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.930
hey, that's equal to something.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.410
Now, what does that equal to?

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:46.270
That's equal to six
times as many as eight.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.450
Well, what's another way to write

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.080
six times as many as eight?

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.130
Well, we can write that
as six times eight.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.170
So this right over here,

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.950
this is that comparison

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.070
written as a multiplication equation.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.340
That's all they're asking for.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.880
And so you would type
that in right over there.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.130
Let's do another example.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:06.550
Here, we are told, or we are asked,

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:09.330
what statement represents the equation

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.400
seven times four is equal to 28?

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.380
So, pause this video

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.940
and think about which
choice would you pick.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:17.773
So, let's see.

00:01:17.773 --> 00:01:21.940
Choice A says, 28 is seven more than four.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.020
First of all, that's not true.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.050
28 is not seven more than four.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.380
But if you were to write this
comparison as an equation,

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.510
this would be that 28 is,

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.510
so is equal to seven more than four

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.090
is seven plus four.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.280
Not only is that not true,

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.880
but that's not the original equation.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.430
So we rule that out.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:43.570
28 is seven times as many as four.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.410
Well, this is interesting.

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:45.640
28,

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.220
28 is,

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.460
is equal to

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.720
seven times as many as four,

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.350
seven times four.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:56.410
Well, the only difference
between this and this

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:59.130
is just we've swapped the
sides on the equality,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.140
which is completely okay.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.940
So, 28 is equal to seven times four,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.350
that's the same equation, really,

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.930
as seven times four is equal to 28.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:10.290
So I like this choice.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.680
Now let's just look at the other choices.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.560
Seven is four times as many as 28.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.930
That plays with your head a little bit,

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:18.780
but let's just write it as an equation.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:19.660
Seven

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:21.443
is

00:02:21.443 --> 00:02:23.070
so that would be equal to

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.820
four times as many as 28

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:27.240
that would be four times 28.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.820
One, this is not true.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:32.280
Four times 28 is over a
100, so it's not seven.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.520
But this is also very different
than what we see up here,

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.930
so we'd rule that out.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.030
Seven is four less than 28.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.100
Well, this equation would be

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.580
seven is,

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.580
so is equal to,

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.760
four less than 28,

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.340
so four less than 28
would be 28 minus four.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.050
Once again, not only is this not true,

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:52.210
28 minus four is 24, not seven,

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.030
but this is not that original equation.

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.430
So we'd rule that one out as well.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.173
So we like our choice B.

